// Detailed visual mnemonics for the 84 N5 Explorer characters plus 帰, used in linked study text.
// These are learner-created visual associations, not claims about character etymology.
globalThis.SAKURA_KANJI_MEMORY=Object.freeze({
  "日":{summary:"Picture 日 as a small sun-window: its frame holds a bright line of sunlight across the middle.",parts:[{glyph:"囗","label":"Sun’s outline","description":"The four outer strokes make a little rectangular sun disk; picture it as the bright face of the sun."},{glyph:"一","label":"Sunbeam","description":"The horizontal middle stroke is a beam of light cutting through the disk."}],story:"At dawn, look through a bright window: the round sun has become a square outline, and one ray shines straight across it. That simple sun picture helps you remember 日 as sun, day, or the day counter."},
  "一":{summary:"One level stroke makes 一: imagine a single horizon line with nothing beside it.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"One line","description":"A single horizontal stroke is the whole character."},{glyph:"—","label":"A count of one","description":"The empty space around the stroke keeps the picture uncluttered: there is only one."}],story:"Draw one clean line across an empty page. There is no second line above or below it, so the picture holds onto the idea of one. When you see 一 in a number or word, recall that single mark."},
  "国":{summary:"The border 囗 surrounds 玉, a precious jewel, like a country protecting what is inside its borders.",parts:[{glyph:"囗","label":"Enclosing border","description":"The large outer square looks like a boundary drawn around a place."},{glyph:"玉","label":"Jewel inside","description":"Inside is 玉, the jewel character: a king-like shape with a small dot."}],story:"Imagine a map with a bold border around a country. Inside the border, a precious jewel is safely kept. The enclosing shape and the protected treasure make a clear picture for 国, a country."},
  "人":{summary:"The two strokes of 人 lean together like a person balancing on two legs.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"First leg","description":"The left-falling stroke leans away like one leg stepping forward."},{glyph:"乀","label":"Second leg","description":"The longer right-falling stroke braces the figure like the other leg."}],story:"Picture two legs leaning apart to support a standing person. The short stroke reaches one way and the longer stroke reaches the other, so the tiny figure can balance. That walking silhouette is 人, a person."},
  "年":{summary:"Stacked strokes in 年 look like the marks of a crop growing through a year, from planting to harvest.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"First mark","description":"The short top stroke begins the stack, like the first mark on a calendar."},{glyph:"十","label":"Crossing seasons","description":"The crossing middle lines form a central marker, dividing the year into stages."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Long timeline","description":"The vertical stroke runs through the stack like time passing from one season to the next."}],story:"Imagine making a tall calendar mark for a growing season: first a small mark, then a cross for the turning point, and finally a line that carries the count downward. The stacked shape reminds you of a year passing from planting to harvest."},
  "大":{summary:"A person-shaped 大 spreads both arms and legs wide to show something large.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Outstretched arms","description":"The long horizontal stroke stretches left and right like a person opening both arms."},{glyph:"人","label":"Standing body","description":"The central and lower strokes make a person with legs planted apart."}],story:"Picture a person standing in the middle of a field and stretching both arms as far as possible. The broad arm line and wide stance fill the space around the figure. This is an easy way to remember 大 as big or large."},
  "十":{summary:"A vertical stroke crosses a horizontal stroke in 十, making a simple mark for ten.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Crossbar","description":"The horizontal stroke is the crossbar."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Upright stroke","description":"The vertical stroke passes through the crossbar."}],story:"Lay one straight stick across another at the center. Together they make a compact cross that is easy to count and spot. Keep that crossed shape in mind for 十, ten, and for the ten-day counter in words such as 十日."},
  "二":{summary:"Two parallel lines make 二: count the upper line, then the lower line.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Upper line","description":"The first horizontal stroke is one."},{glyph:"一","label":"Lower line","description":"A second parallel stroke adds one more."}],story:"Draw a line, then draw another underneath it. The pair stays parallel and evenly separated, making the number visible at a glance. Two horizontal marks are 二, two."},
  "本":{summary:"本 is a tree 木 with a marker at its base: find the root or starting point of a book’s knowledge.",parts:[{glyph:"木","label":"Tree","description":"The vertical trunk, side branches, and lower roots form 木, a tree."},{glyph:"一","label":"Root marker","description":"The short line across the lower trunk points to the tree’s base, its origin."}],story:"Picture a tree with its roots firmly in the soil. A small marker crosses the trunk right where the roots begin, showing the base or source. A book is a starting place for knowledge, so this root-marked tree helps recall 本."},
  "中":{summary:"A vertical line passes through the center of a box in 中, pointing to the middle or inside.",parts:[{glyph:"口","label":"Box","description":"The outer square resembles a container or enclosed space."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Center line","description":"The vertical stroke passes through the box’s center."}],story:"Draw a box and run a straight line through its exact middle. The line touches the space inside and divides it evenly, so the picture points to center, middle, or inside. That is the shape of 中."},
  "長":{summary:"Long sweeping strokes in 長 stretch from a compact top to a broad lower sweep, like something extending far.",parts:[{glyph:"長","label":"Lengthening strokes","description":"The vertical strokes build a tall shape, while the sweeping lower stroke reaches outward."},{glyph:"一","label":"Extended path","description":"The broad lower line gives the picture a visible direction and distance."}],story:"Imagine a path beginning high on a hill and sweeping far across the ground. Your eyes travel down the tall strokes and then follow the long final sweep. That extended journey helps remember 長 as long, or a leader who stands out ahead."},
  "出":{summary:"Two mountain-like forms stack in 出, with one rising out from behind the other.",parts:[{glyph:"山","label":"Front peak","description":"The lower part resembles a small mountain with a center peak."},{glyph:"山","label":"Peak behind","description":"A second mountain-like shape rises above the first."}],story:"Imagine climbing through a valley between two mountain ridges. You pass the nearer ridge and emerge above it, with another peak appearing behind. The stacked peaks create the motion of coming out or leaving: 出."},
  "三":{summary:"Three horizontal strokes make 三; count them from top to bottom.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"First line","description":"The top horizontal stroke is one."},{glyph:"一","label":"Second line","description":"The middle stroke is two."},{glyph:"一","label":"Third line","description":"The bottom stroke is three."}],story:"Stack three short shelves, one above another, and count each shelf as your eyes move downward. Nothing is hidden or joined; the three marks tell you the number directly. This is 三, three."},
  "時":{summary:"The sun 日 beside the temple 寺 marks the hours as sunlight passes the temple.",parts:[{glyph:"日","label":"Sun / daylight","description":"The left-hand 日 is the sun, a frame with a bright line inside."},{glyph:"寺","label":"Temple","description":"The right-hand 寺 has a roof-like top and 土-like base; picture a temple where people watch the day pass."}],story:"Imagine standing beside a temple and checking the sunlight on its wall. As the bright patch moves, you know another hour has passed. The sun 日 beside the temple 寺 gives a memorable scene for 時, time or hour."},
  "行":{summary:"行 looks like two sides of a crossing road, inviting you to walk from one side to the other.",parts:[{glyph:"彳","label":"Left-hand path","description":"The left side has the small step-like strokes of a walking path."},{glyph:"亍","label":"Right-hand path","description":"The right side continues the crossing with another pair of road-like strokes."}],story:"Picture a person reaching a crossroads. One path comes from the left, another continues on the right, and you choose a direction and set off. The street-like shape helps remember 行 as going, a journey, or carrying something out."},
  "見":{summary:"An eye 目 stands on two legs 儿 in 見, ready to look at what is ahead.",parts:[{glyph:"目","label":"Eye","description":"The upper box with inner lines is 目, an eye looking straight ahead."},{glyph:"儿","label":"Two legs","description":"The two lower strokes look like legs that carry the eye toward what it sees."}],story:"Imagine an enormous eye standing on two legs. It can walk over to a scene, stop, and look carefully. The eye 目 supported by legs 儿 is a picture for 見, to see or look."},
  "月":{summary:"The curved outline of 月 resembles a crescent moon, a shape people use to mark each month.",parts:[{glyph:"月","label":"Moon outline","description":"The outer strokes form a curved crescent-like body."},{glyph:"二","label":"Light bands","description":"The inner horizontal marks suggest bands of moonlight across the shape."}],story:"Picture a crescent moon with two thin bands of light across its face. Watch it change through the night sky and return again next month. The curved moon shape links 月 to moon and month."},
  "分":{summary:"The dividing mark 八 sits over a knife 刀 in 分, as if a blade splits something into parts.",parts:[{glyph:"八","label":"Split / divide","description":"The two upper strokes open away from each other like something being separated."},{glyph:"刀","label":"Knife","description":"The lower shape is a blade used to cut one thing into sections."}],story:"Place a piece of fruit on a board and use a knife to cut it in two. The upper strokes spread apart to show the split, while the lower shape supplies the cutting tool. This picture helps remember 分 as part, divide, or a minute on the clock."},
  "後":{summary:"A small walking step 彳 comes first, then a trailing shape, as if someone is following behind.",parts:[{glyph:"彳","label":"Walking steps","description":"The left-side strokes resemble the small steps of a person walking."},{glyph:"幺","label":"Trailing thread","description":"The upper-right curves look like a short thread or loop trailing after the walker."},{glyph:"夂","label":"Footstep behind","description":"The lower-right strokes bend back like a final step following the others."}],story:"Imagine following someone down a path. Their first steps move ahead, and the last footprint stays behind you; after that, more time has passed. The trailing pieces beside the walking-step shape make 後 mean behind, later, or after."},
  "前":{summary:"In 前, the body-like top advances over a pair of cutting strokes, like feet stepping to the front.",parts:[{glyph:"月","label":"Forward body","description":"The upper-left shape resembles a body leaning toward the way ahead."},{glyph:"䒑","label":"Forward motion","description":"The short top strokes suggest the start of a stride."},{glyph:"刂","label":"Two leading marks","description":"The two upright strokes at the bottom make a pair of marks at the front edge."}],story:"Picture a person leaning forward and placing both feet just ahead of the starting line. The broad upper shape moves over a pair of upright marks, so your eyes see something at the front. This scene helps remember 前 as in front or before."},
  "生":{summary:"生 looks like a living shoot pushing up through the ground, with leaves reaching toward the sky.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Growing stem","description":"The central vertical stroke is a stem rising upward."},{glyph:"一","label":"Ground line","description":"The horizontal mark near the bottom is the soil surface the shoot pushes through."},{glyph:"𠂉","label":"New leaves","description":"The top strokes spread like the first leaves of a plant."}],story:"Imagine a fresh green shoot breaking through the soil. Its stem rises through the ground line and opens into new leaves at the top. The whole form is alive and growing, helping you recall 生 for life, birth, or being a student."},
  "五":{summary:"The crossing and turning strokes of 五 look like five tally marks compressed into one character.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Top tally","description":"The upper horizontal stroke begins the count."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Crossing stroke","description":"The center stroke joins the top and lower sections."},{glyph:"乚","label":"Turned lower mark","description":"The bent lower strokes complete the compact tally."}],story:"Count five marks on one hand, then imagine them folded into a compact sign: one bar at the top, a center post, and a bent base. The crossed, turning shape becomes your visual cue for 五, five."},
  "間":{summary:"A gate 門 frames the sun 日 shining through an opening in 間, making a space or interval.",parts:[{glyph:"門","label":"Gate","description":"The two tall outer sides look like a pair of doors around an opening."},{glyph:"日","label":"Sun through the gate","description":"The sun sits inside the opening, visible between the doorposts."}],story:"Stand outside a gate and watch the sun through the gap between its doors. The open distance between the frame and the passing daylight is a space; the time between two sunrises is an interval. That gate-and-sun scene helps remember 間."},
  "上":{summary:"A short mark sits above the long baseline in 上, so the picture literally points upward.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Baseline","description":"The long horizontal stroke is the surface or level you compare against."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Point above","description":"The upright stroke rises from the baseline, and its short cap sits above it."}],story:"Draw a long floor line, then place a short mark above it. The mark is visibly higher than the level beneath, so your eyes do not have to guess the direction. This arrangement is 上, above or up."},
  "東":{summary:"A bright sun 日 appears through the branches of 木 in 東, where sunrise begins in the east.",parts:[{glyph:"日","label":"Sun","description":"The center box is a sun with a bright line inside it."},{glyph:"木","label":"Tree / branches","description":"The surrounding and lower strokes suggest branches and a trunk framing the sun."}],story:"Imagine early morning: a bright sun rises through the branches of a tree. Its light appears first at the eastern edge of the sky. The sun caught among tree-like strokes makes 東 easy to remember as east."},
  "四":{summary:"The outside of 四 makes a four-cornered frame; picture four things sitting inside it.",parts:[{glyph:"囗","label":"Four-sided frame","description":"The outer strokes mark the corners and walls of a square."},{glyph:"儿","label":"Inside shapes","description":"The inner strokes can be imagined as two small forms tucked into the frame."}],story:"Put four small stones inside a square tray, one for each corner. The frame holds the count together while your eyes move around all four sides. This box-like picture helps remember 四, four."},
  "今":{summary:"A roof-like top 𠆢 shelters a folded mark in 今, like the present moment held under a cover.",parts:[{glyph:"𠆢","label":"Cover / roof","description":"The two sloping top strokes meet like a small roof over the character."},{glyph:"フ","label":"Folded moment","description":"The lower bent stroke looks like a page corner folded to mark the point you are at now."}],story:"Imagine a roof sheltering one folded page in a calendar. The fold marks exactly where you are standing today; yesterday and tomorrow are outside the shelter. That marked present moment helps you remember 今, now."},
  "金":{summary:"A roof-like cover shelters bright metal pieces in 金, like gold kept safely in a treasure chest.",parts:[{glyph:"𠆢","label":"Chest lid","description":"The two top strokes form a peaked cover over what lies beneath."},{glyph:"王","label":"Stacked treasure","description":"The central crossed lines resemble a neatly stacked bar or block of metal."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Glint","description":"The small lower marks sparkle like reflections from gold."}],story:"Picture a treasure chest with a pointed lid. Inside are stacked bars of metal, and tiny glints shine near the bottom when the lid opens. The covered treasure scene connects 金 with gold, metal, and money."},
  "九":{summary:"The curved hook in 九 feels like the final bent tally before a count reaches ten.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"First tally","description":"The short diagonal begins the mark."},{glyph:"乙","label":"Curved hook","description":"The longer stroke bends and hooks, like a tally turning at its end."}],story:"Count along a row of marks and imagine the ninth one bending into a hook just before the next mark would make ten. Its curved ending is the detail to remember. That hooked tally is 九, nine."},
  "入":{summary:"Two slanting strokes narrow toward the top in 入, like someone passing through a doorway.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"Left door edge","description":"The longer left-falling stroke angles inward like one side of a narrow entrance."},{glyph:"乀","label":"Right door edge","description":"The shorter right-falling stroke meets it, leaving a path into the space."}],story:"Picture a doorway that narrows toward the inside. A person steps between the slanting sides and passes through rather than away from them. That inward movement helps you remember 入 as enter or put in."},
  "学":{summary:"A child 子 learns beneath the sheltering top strokes of 学, like a student sitting under a school roof.",parts:[{glyph:"⺍","label":"Roof beams","description":"The top strokes spread like a small roof or canopy over the character."},{glyph:"冖","label":"Shelter","description":"The middle cover rests over the child below."},{glyph:"子","label":"Child / learner","description":"The lower shape is 子, a child with a head and a small body."}],story:"Imagine a child sitting under a school roof with a book open. The roof shelters the learner, and the child shape at the bottom keeps the scene grounded. A child learning under cover is an easy picture for 学, study or learning."},
  "高":{summary:"A tall building in 高 stacks rooms between a roof and a broad base, so the whole character rises upward.",parts:[{glyph:"亠","label":"Roof","description":"The top cap makes a roof above the building."},{glyph:"口","label":"Upper window","description":"The first square looks like a room or window high in the building."},{glyph:"冂","label":"Outer walls","description":"The broad outer frame encloses the lower rooms."},{glyph:"口","label":"Lower room","description":"The second square is another enclosed room in the tower."}],story:"Look up at a tall building: a roof sits over one window, the walls continue downward, and another room is enclosed near the base. Your eyes climb through the stacked levels. That vertical tower picture helps remember 高 as high or tall."},
  "円":{summary:"The angular frame of 円 encloses a few marks like a coin held inside a stamped border.",parts:[{glyph:"冂","label":"Outer coin rim","description":"The enclosing strokes make a squared frame around the inner marks; picture it as a coin drawn inside a border."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Coin detail","description":"The inner stroke divides the face of the coin into a visible mark."}],story:"Picture a coin held inside a complete frame. Its rim surrounds the value stamped in the middle, and the enclosed shape feels complete. This coin-like picture helps remember 円 as circle and as yen.",words:[{word:"円",reading:"えん",meaning:"yen"}]},
  "子":{summary:"The short top and spreading lower strokes of 子 make a small child with arms and legs open.",parts:[{glyph:"フ","label":"Head and arms","description":"The top bent stroke looks like a child’s head with one arm reaching out."},{glyph:"一","label":"Outstretched arm","description":"The horizontal stroke reaches across like a small arm."},{glyph:"亅","label":"Body and leg","description":"The long lower stroke drops and turns like a little body standing on one leg."}],story:"Imagine a small child reaching both arms outward and planting one foot on the floor. The top is a head, the middle reaches like an arm, and the long lower line bends into a leg. This child silhouette is 子."},
  "外":{summary:"The evening crescent 夕 sits beside a fortune-telling mark 卜 in 外, away from the bright center.",parts:[{glyph:"夕","label":"Evening sky","description":"The left strokes resemble 夕, an evening sky with a crescent moon."},{glyph:"卜","label":"Mark beyond","description":"The upright and dot on the right look like a marker placed outside the main scene."}],story:"Imagine leaving the house after sunset. A crescent hangs in the evening sky, and a signpost points beyond the doorway to the world outside. The moon-at-evening beside a marker helps you remember 外, outside."},
  "八":{summary:"The two strokes of 八 open away from each other like a split pair; that pair is eight.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"Left stroke","description":"The left stroke falls outward."},{glyph:"乀","label":"Right stroke","description":"The right stroke falls the other way, leaving a gap between the pair."}],story:"Take one bundle and split it into two equal groups; each side opens away from the center. The two spreading strokes make that split visible. Keep the open pair in mind for 八, eight."},
  "六":{summary:"A small roof 亠 sits over two spreading strokes 八 in 六, sheltering six things underneath.",parts:[{glyph:"亠","label":"Small roof","description":"The upper cap resembles a little roof."},{glyph:"八","label":"Two open marks","description":"The lower strokes spread apart like a pair beneath the roof."}],story:"Picture a little roof over a pair of open hands. Count three small objects in each hand: together they make six beneath the shelter. The roof above the two spreading strokes gives you a distinct cue for 六."},
  "下":{summary:"In 下, a short mark hangs below the long baseline, pointing to the lower side.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Top surface","description":"The long horizontal stroke is a shelf or level."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Line through the level","description":"The vertical line drops below the surface."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Lower mark","description":"The small mark sits under the line, visibly below the baseline."}],story:"Draw a shelf, drop a line through it, and place a small dot underneath. The dot cannot be mistaken for something above the shelf; it is clearly on the lower side. This arrangement helps remember 下, below or down."},
  "来":{summary:"The central trunk and side strokes in 来 look like a tree offering branches and grain as something comes toward you.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Central trunk","description":"The vertical center is a trunk rising through the character."},{glyph:"一","label":"Branch line","description":"The horizontal strokes spread across like branches."},{glyph:"米","label":"Grain-like lower strokes","description":"The lower diagonals look like small grains or branches reaching outward."}],story:"Imagine a fruit tree leaning over a path. Its branches spread toward you and offer something as you walk closer. The central trunk with reaching side strokes gives a welcoming picture for 来, to come."},
  "気":{summary:"The airy top 气 swirls above the bright marks below in 気, like energy rising through the air.",parts:[{glyph:"气","label":"Air / vapor","description":"The upper strokes curve like wisps of air moving across the sky."},{glyph:"米","label":"Small sparks","description":"The lower crossed marks can be imagined as tiny sparks or grains that make the air lively."}],story:"Picture a breeze lifting a few sparks from the ground and swirling them into the air. The moving vapor above and lively marks below make an invisible force feel visible. This image helps remember 気 as spirit, feeling, or energy."},
  "小":{summary:"A long center stroke and two tiny side marks make 小, a large line surrounded by little pieces.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Center stroke","description":"The middle stroke is the main line of the character."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Small side marks","description":"The two short marks on either side look like tiny pieces beside the center."}],story:"Imagine one long stick with two tiny pebbles beside it. The center is clear and tall, while the side marks are small. That contrast between the main line and little marks helps you recall 小 as small or little."},
  "七":{summary:"The straight top stroke in 七 turns into a hook, like a tally mark bending at number seven.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Top tally","description":"The horizontal stroke begins like a count mark."},{glyph:"乚","label":"Bent hook","description":"The lower stroke bends sharply and hooks like a tally turning downward."}],story:"Count marks across a page and imagine the seventh one changing direction at the end. It starts straight, then turns down and hooks back. That distinct turn is the visual clue for 七, seven."},
  "山":{summary:"山 is three mountain peaks: the tall center peak stands between two shorter ridges.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Middle peak","description":"The central vertical stroke rises highest, like the main summit."},{glyph:"凵","label":"Two side ridges","description":"The outer strokes form lower shoulders on both sides of the central peak."}],story:"Picture three mountain peaks in a row. The middle summit rises tall, while two lower ridges sit on its left and right. The three-part skyline is the character 山, a mountain."},
  "話":{summary:"Words 言 meet a tongue-like 舌 in 話, making a spoken story or conversation.",parts:[{glyph:"言","label":"Words / speech","description":"The left component is 言, the speech marks used in many language kanji."},{glyph:"舌","label":"Tongue","description":"The right component is 舌, a tongue with a broad shape and a pointed lower stroke."}],story:"Imagine words forming on one side and a tongue speaking them on the other. The tongue turns thoughts into a spoken story that another person can hear. Words 言 beside tongue 舌 make a picture for 話, talk, story, or speaking."},
  "女":{summary:"The crossed and curved strokes of 女 suggest a seated figure with arms folded in front.",parts:[{glyph:"𡿨","label":"Seated outline","description":"The curved stroke gives the figure a bent, seated posture."},{glyph:"一","label":"Folded arm","description":"The crossing horizontal stroke suggests an arm resting across the body."},{glyph:"丿","label":"Second arm / leg","description":"The long slant completes the compact human figure."}],story:"Picture a person sitting with knees bent and arms folded comfortably in front. One curved stroke forms the seated outline, and the crossing lines make the pose. This little figure is a visual reminder for 女, woman or female."},
  "北":{summary:"Two figures in 北 turn their backs away from each other, facing opposite directions on a map.",parts:[{glyph:"匕","label":"Left-facing figure","description":"The left part looks like a person turned around, with a bent body and head."},{glyph:"匕","label":"Right-facing figure","description":"The matching right part faces the other way, showing two backs turned apart."}],story:"Imagine two travelers standing back-to-back at the top of a map. One looks east and the other west, but both keep the cold northern wind behind them. Their paired backs create a cue for 北, north."},
  "午":{summary:"A short mark crosses the upright middle of 午, like the sun reaching its high noon position.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Sun’s path","description":"The long vertical stroke marks a straight path through the sky."},{glyph:"十","label":"Crossing point","description":"The crossed center makes the position where the sun stands highest."},{glyph:"ノ","label":"Top mark","description":"The small upper stroke points to the bright point at the top of the day."}],story:"Picture the sun traveling upward along a line until it reaches the crossing point at the middle of the sky. At that moment the day is at noon. The short mark above and crossing center help remember 午, noon."},
  "百":{summary:"A single mark 一 sits over 白, making one complete hundred-count above a bright group.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"One","description":"The top horizontal stroke means one in the visual picture."},{glyph:"白","label":"Bright counted group","description":"The lower shape resembles 白, a bright sun-like box with a small glint."}],story:"Imagine one bright tray holding a complete set of counted objects. The single line above announces one full group, and the bright box below holds the count. This picture links 百 to one hundred."},
  "書":{summary:"A brush-like hand 聿 lays strokes across a page in 書, leaving written marks behind.",parts:[{glyph:"聿","label":"Writing brush","description":"The upper strokes look like a brush handle held upright, with crossbars for the grip."},{glyph:"曰","label":"Page / writing space","description":"The lower box resembles a page or panel where the brush leaves a mark."}],story:"Imagine holding a brush by its crossbars and writing across a clean page. The handle guides the strokes while the lower panel receives each mark. A brush working on a page is a clear memory for 書, write or writing."},
  "先":{summary:"A person 儿 steps past the line above in 先, moving ahead of the others.",parts:[{glyph:"土","label":"Starting ground","description":"The upper crossed strokes make a small platform or starting point."},{glyph:"儿","label":"Person stepping ahead","description":"The lower strokes form a person with legs moving forward."}],story:"Picture a person reaching a small starting line and taking one step beyond it. The feet pass ahead of the mark before anyone else. This forward step helps you remember 先 as before, ahead, or earlier."},
  "名":{summary:"At evening 夕, a mouth 口 calls out to learn someone’s name in 名.",parts:[{glyph:"夕","label":"Evening","description":"The top component is 夕, a crescent in the evening sky."},{glyph:"口","label":"Calling mouth","description":"The lower square is a mouth speaking a question."}],story:"Imagine meeting someone after sunset. You cannot see their face clearly, so you call out and ask their name. The evening shape 夕 sits over a speaking mouth 口, making 名 a memorable sign for name."},
  "川":{summary:"Three long strokes in 川 flow side by side like channels of a river.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Left stream","description":"The left line is one narrow stream."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Middle stream","description":"The central line flows straight down the valley."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Right stream","description":"The right line is a third channel beside the others."}],story:"Picture standing on a bridge above three streams flowing in parallel. Each long stroke is a channel, and the gaps between them are water paths. The side-by-side flow makes 川 an easy picture for river."},
  "千":{summary:"A small diagonal ノ joins 十 in 千, adding a marker to ten to make one thousand.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"Added mark","description":"The short diagonal at the top is an extra counting mark."},{glyph:"十","label":"Ten","description":"The crossed lower shape is 十, the familiar sign for ten."}],story:"Imagine making ten groups of ten, then ten more groups: your count grows into a thousand. A small mark joins the familiar crossed ten below, making one compact sign for the larger count. This is 千, one thousand."},
  "水":{summary:"A central stream falls through 水 while short side strokes splash out like water droplets.",parts:[{glyph:"亅","label":"Main stream","description":"The long center stroke flows downward and bends at the bottom."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Left splash","description":"The short left mark flicks outward like a drop."},{glyph:"丿","label":"Right splash","description":"The longer side stroke sprays away from the stream."}],story:"Picture a stream falling over a rock. A strong central ribbon of water drops down while small splashes flick out on both sides. That central flow and scattering drops make 水 a vivid picture for water."},
  "半":{summary:"A center line divides a whole stack into two sides in 半, leaving one half on either side.",parts:[{glyph:"二","label":"Two levels","description":"The upper horizontal strokes form two layers of a whole."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Dividing line","description":"The center line runs through the layers and splits them."},{glyph:"八","label":"Two halves","description":"The lower strokes open away from each other like the separated sides."}],story:"Imagine a cake with two layers cut straight down the middle. The center line divides the whole, and the lower sides spread apart to show the pieces. This divided shape helps you remember 半, half."},
  "男":{summary:"A field 田 sits above strength 力 in 男, picturing someone using strength to work the land.",parts:[{glyph:"田","label":"Field","description":"The upper box is a field divided into small plots."},{glyph:"力","label":"Strength","description":"The lower hooked strokes make 力, a person exerting strength."}],story:"Picture a farmer in a divided field, pushing a tool through the soil with strength. The field 田 is above and the working force 力 is below. This scene makes 男 easier to remember as man or male."},
  "西":{summary:"A covered container encloses its contents in 西, like the sun settling into a western horizon box.",parts:[{glyph:"覀","label":"Covering frame","description":"The upper and side strokes form a roof-like enclosure."},{glyph:"儿","label":"Contents inside","description":"The lower strokes sit within the frame like the last light tucked into it."}],story:"Imagine the sun sinking into a covered box at the edge of the map. The lid and sides close around the last bright light as evening arrives. That sunset-at-the-edge scene helps remember 西, west."},
  "電":{summary:"Rain 雨 hangs above the lightning-shaped lower form in 電, like a flash of electricity in a storm.",parts:[{glyph:"雨","label":"Rain cloud","description":"The top enclosure and four drops make 雨, rain falling from a cloud."},{glyph:"申","label":"Lightning flash","description":"The lower vertical shape with crossbars looks like a sharp bolt cutting through the storm."}],story:"Picture a heavy rain cloud opening above a field. A jagged flash shoots downward through the rain, briefly lighting everything around it. Rain 雨 over a lightning mark makes 電 a memorable picture for electricity."},
  "無":{summary:"Busy strokes in 無 fill the upper space, while the lower line leaves an empty patch where nothing remains.",parts:[{glyph:"𠂉","label":"Scattered traces","description":"The upper strokes spread like many things moving around."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Clearing line","description":"The long center stroke sweeps through the busy area."},{glyph:"灬","label":"Last sparks","description":"The bottom dots are the last sparks fading away."}],story:"Imagine a room full of objects. A sweeping motion moves them out, and the last little sparks or dust marks fade at the bottom. When the busy picture has been cleared away, nothing remains. That empty ending helps remember 無, none or nothing."},
  "校":{summary:"A tree 木 stands beside people crossing paths 交 in 校, a place where learners meet.",parts:[{glyph:"木","label":"Tree / wood","description":"The left component has a trunk and branches like a tree."},{glyph:"交","label":"Paths meeting","description":"The right component has crossing strokes above spread legs, like paths meeting at a place."}],story:"Imagine a schoolyard beneath a tree where students arrive from crossing paths and meet their classmates. The tree 木 marks the left side, and the crossing paths 交 form the meeting place. That gathering scene helps recall 校, school."},
  "語":{summary:"Speech 言 joins 吾, the speaker’s self, in 語: words are what I say to another person.",parts:[{glyph:"言","label":"Speech / words","description":"The left side is 言, the speech component used in language characters."},{glyph:"吾","label":"I / my voice","description":"The right side contains 五-like crossed marks above 口, a mouth speaking as ‘I’."}],story:"Picture a person opening their mouth to say words about themselves. Speech 言 joins a speaking self 吾, turning a thought into language another person can understand. This scene helps remember 語, word or language."},
  "土":{summary:"A short ground mark sits above the broad base in 土, like a small mound of soil on the earth.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Top of the mound","description":"The shorter upper line is the top surface of the pile."},{glyph:"丨","label":"Mound’s center","description":"The vertical stroke runs down through its center."},{glyph:"一","label":"Ground","description":"The broad lower line is the earth supporting the mound."}],story:"Picture a mound of soil rising from a wide patch of ground. A small line marks its top, a center line shows its height, and the broad base holds it steady. This little earth mound is 土, soil or ground."},
  "木":{summary:"A vertical trunk, two branches, and spreading roots make a complete tree in 木.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Trunk","description":"The long center stroke is the tree’s trunk."},{glyph:"丿","label":"Left branch","description":"The left-falling stroke reaches out like a branch."},{glyph:"乀","label":"Right branch","description":"The right-falling stroke mirrors it on the other side."},{glyph:"一","label":"Roots","description":"The lower cross-stroke spreads like roots into the ground."}],story:"Imagine a tree viewed from the front: a straight trunk rises, two branches reach to the sides, and roots spread along the soil. The full plant silhouette is simple to recognize. This is 木, tree or wood."},
  "聞":{summary:"An ear 耳 listens through the gate 門 in 聞, hearing what passes on the other side.",parts:[{glyph:"門","label":"Gate","description":"The two upright outer strokes make a doorway or gate."},{glyph:"耳","label":"Ear","description":"The inner shape is 耳, an ear with folds that catch sound."}],story:"Stand at a closed gate and put your ear against it. Voices and footsteps pass through from the other side, even though you cannot see them. The ear 耳 inside the gate 門 gives a direct picture for 聞, hear or ask."},
  "食":{summary:"A covered meal in 食 has a roof-like top over the food waiting underneath.",parts:[{glyph:"𠆢","label":"Meal cover","description":"The upper strokes meet like a lid or roof covering a dish."},{glyph:"良","label":"Food beneath","description":"The lower body narrows toward the bottom like food gathered on a spoon or held for a meal."}],story:"Picture a warm bowl brought to the table under a lid. Lift the cover and find food waiting beneath; the shape narrows as if the meal is gathered up for a bite. This covered meal helps remember 食, eat or food."},
  "車":{summary:"車 is a cart seen from above, with a central axle, a frame, and wheels on both sides.",parts:[{glyph:"丨","label":"Axle","description":"The central vertical stroke runs through the vehicle like its axle."},{glyph:"一","label":"Crossbars","description":"The horizontal lines brace the frame across the axle."},{glyph:"冂","label":"Cart frame","description":"The surrounding strokes suggest the body of a cart."}],story:"Look down at a small cart from overhead. Its long axle runs through the middle, crossbars hold the frame together, and wheels sit on either side. That top-down vehicle drawing is 車, car or vehicle."},
  "何":{summary:"A person 亻 stands beside 可, asking what can be done in 何.",parts:[{glyph:"亻","label":"Person","description":"The left-side person radical is a small standing figure."},{glyph:"可","label":"Question space","description":"The right component has a mouth-like box and a stroke above it, like a sign waiting for an answer."}],story:"Imagine a person stopping at a sign and asking what it means. The standing person 亻 is next to a marked question space 可, so the whole character prompts you to ask ‘what?’ This is 何."},
  "南":{summary:"The enclosed center of 南 looks like a marked place on a map, with its direction pointing toward the bottom edge.",parts:[{glyph:"冂","label":"Map frame","description":"The outer top and sides create a frame like the edge of a map."},{glyph:"𠂉","label":"Direction marker","description":"The center strokes gather around a marker in the middle of the frame."},{glyph:"十","label":"Crossroads","description":"The lower crossing lines resemble a map grid or compass intersection."}],story:"Imagine a map framed at the top with a compass marker in the center. Follow its pointer down toward the bottom edge to find the warm southern side. The framed center and lower crossing help you remember 南, south."},
  "万":{summary:"The top stroke and long bent sweep of 万 stretch across a very large count: ten thousand.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Top line","description":"The upper stroke begins the sign like a cap over the count."},{glyph:"𠃌","label":"Wide bend","description":"The long hooked stroke curves across and down, reaching far beyond the top mark."}],story:"Picture a counter writing a number so large that the final stroke sweeps far across the page and hooks down at the end. The long reach makes the count feel enormous. This wide bent mark helps remember 万, ten thousand."},
  "毎":{summary:"The top mark in 毎 rests over 母, like a familiar routine repeated by a parent every day.",parts:[{glyph:"𠂉","label":"Repeated mark","description":"The top short strokes mark the start of the repeated pattern."},{glyph:"母","label":"Mother / home routine","description":"The lower shape resembles 母, a familiar figure at home."}],story:"Imagine a mother checking the same calendar at breakfast every morning. The small mark above reminds you that the routine repeats, while 母 below anchors the scene at home. A regular pattern that returns each day helps recall 毎, every."},
  "白":{summary:"A small glint ノ sits on a bright sun box 日 in 白, making the whole shape shine white.",parts:[{glyph:"ノ","label":"Glint of light","description":"The small diagonal stroke is a sparkle on the surface."},{glyph:"日","label":"Bright sun box","description":"The box below resembles 日, a sun with a bright line inside."}],story:"Imagine a bright sun reflecting from a clean white surface. A small glint catches your eye above the sun-shaped box, making the whole picture shine. The flash of brightness helps you remember 白, white."},
  "天":{summary:"A person 大 reaches above the line in 天, stretching toward the open sky overhead.",parts:[{glyph:"大","label":"Person with arms wide","description":"The lower shape is 大, a person spreading arms and legs."},{glyph:"一","label":"Sky line","description":"The short top line marks the space above the person’s reach."}],story:"Picture a person standing with arms wide and reaching over a high horizon line. Above that line is the open sky, far beyond the person’s head. A person 大 reaching toward the upper line gives a picture for 天, sky or heaven."},
  "母":{summary:"The enclosing strokes and two inner dots in 母 suggest a mother holding and nourishing a child.",parts:[{glyph:"凵","label":"Protective arms","description":"The outer bends wrap around the center like arms enclosing someone."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Two nourishing marks","description":"The two inner dots are small, memorable details held inside the enclosure."}],story:"Imagine a mother wrapping both arms around a child and offering food and care. The outer shape holds the center safely, and the two small marks stay inside the embrace. This caring picture helps remember 母, mother."},
  "火":{summary:"A central flame in 火 sends two sparks outward, as if a small fire is flickering.",parts:[{glyph:"丿","label":"Left flame","description":"The left-falling stroke flickers away from the center."},{glyph:"人","label":"Flame body","description":"The central strokes rise and split like the body of a flame."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Right spark","description":"The short mark is a spark flying off to the side."}],story:"Picture a campfire with one tall central flame. A gust pushes a spark to the left and another flicker to the right. The bright center and scattered sparks form 火, fire."},
  "右":{summary:"A hand-shaped stroke ナ points toward a mouth 口 in 右, as if giving directions to the right.",parts:[{glyph:"𠂇","label":"Pointing hand","description":"The upper-left strokes suggest an arm and hand extending outward."},{glyph:"口","label":"Speaking mouth","description":"The lower box is a mouth giving the direction aloud."}],story:"Imagine someone raising a hand and pointing while saying, ‘Turn right.’ The hand-like strokes reach toward the side, and the mouth 口 gives the instruction. This gesture helps remember 右, right."},
  "読":{summary:"Speech 言 stands beside 売, like words being read aloud and shared with listeners.",parts:[{glyph:"言","label":"Words / speech","description":"The left component is 言, the familiar speech marks."},{glyph:"売","label":"Shared text","description":"The right component has a roof-like top over a person-like lower shape, suggesting a book or message being passed along."}],story:"Imagine opening a book and speaking its words so another person can hear them. Speech 言 gives voice to the text on the right, and the message moves from page to listener. This shared-words scene helps remember 読, read."},
  "友":{summary:"Two hand-like strokes reach toward each other in 友, meeting to help a friend.",parts:[{glyph:"𠂇","label":"First reaching hand","description":"The upper-left strokes resemble a hand extending outward."},{glyph:"又","label":"Helping hand","description":"The lower component 又 is a hand shape reaching in to meet it."}],story:"Picture two hands reaching from opposite sides and clasping in greeting. One extends first; the other reaches back and offers help. That joined gesture gives a friendly visual memory for 友, friend."},
  "左":{summary:"A hand 𠂇 works beside the square 工 tool in 左, holding a tool on the left side.",parts:[{glyph:"𠂇","label":"Working hand","description":"The upper-left strokes look like a hand reaching toward a task."},{glyph:"工","label":"Tool / work frame","description":"The lower box-like strokes are 工, a tool or workbench shape."}],story:"Imagine using your left hand to hold a tool steady while you work. The hand-like upper strokes sit above the square work shape 工, fixing the tool on one side. This hand-and-tool picture helps distinguish 左, left."},
  "休":{summary:"A person 亻 leans against a tree 木 in 休, pausing under its shade to rest.",parts:[{glyph:"亻","label":"Person","description":"The left component is a small standing person."},{glyph:"木","label":"Tree","description":"The right component has a trunk, branches, and roots like a tree."}],story:"Picture a tired traveler leaning a shoulder against a tree trunk. The branches spread overhead and cast shade while the person pauses. Person 亻 beside tree 木 makes a simple scene for 休, rest or a day off."},
  "父":{summary:"Crossed strokes in 父 resemble tools held in two hands by a father doing a job.",parts:[{glyph:"八","label":"Two raised hands","description":"The upper strokes open apart like arms reaching outward."},{glyph:"乂","label":"Crossed tools","description":"The lower crossing strokes resemble two tools meeting at the center."}],story:"Imagine a father lifting two tools and crossing them briefly before starting work. The open upper strokes are his arms; the crossed lower marks are the tools in his hands. The recognizable gesture helps remember 父, father."},
  "雨":{summary:"A cloud-like cover in 雨 holds four falling drops beneath it.",parts:[{glyph:"一","label":"Cloud roof","description":"The long upper stroke is the top of the cloud."},{glyph:"冂","label":"Cloud body","description":"The enclosure below makes a cloud with a roof and sides."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Raindrops","description":"Four small inner marks fall from the cloud in pairs."}],story:"Picture a heavy cloud hanging low in the sky. Four drops gather underneath and fall in two rows, one after another. The covered cloud and visible droplets make 雨 a direct image for rain."},
  "丈":{summary:"The broad person-like 大 in 丈 gains one extra stroke, as if measuring a person’s full height.",parts:[{glyph:"大","label":"Standing figure","description":"The wide lower strokes resemble a person with arms spread."},{glyph:"丶","label":"Extra measure mark","description":"The additional short stroke marks the figure’s height or reach."}],story:"Imagine measuring a tall person from the floor to the top of a raised hand. The broad figure stands in place while one extra mark records the length. That height-measuring scene helps recall 丈, length or a measure."},
  "誰":{summary:"Words 言 ask who, while 隹 looks like a small bird waiting for its name in 誰.",parts:[{glyph:"言","label":"Question words","description":"The left component is 言, speech used to ask a question."},{glyph:"隹","label":"Small bird","description":"The right component looks like a short-tailed bird perched and waiting."}],story:"Imagine seeing a little bird perched on a branch and asking, ‘Who is that?’ Words 言 form the question beside the waiting bird 隹. This question-and-bird scene helps remember 誰, who."},
  "貼":{summary:"A shell 貝 sits beside 占 in 貼, like a valuable label placed onto a surface.",parts:[{glyph:"貝","label":"Shell / valuable item","description":"The left component is 貝, a shell shape associated with something valuable."},{glyph:"占","label":"Marked place","description":"The right component has a small mark above a box, like a chosen spot or label position."}],story:"Picture choosing a spot on a package and placing a bright label there so the valuable item can be identified. The shell-like 貝 is on one side and the marked place 占 is on the other. That placing action helps recall 貼, stick or paste."},
  "帰":{reading:"かえる (kaeru) · き (ki)",summary:"帰 places a narrow doorway-like 刂 beside a broom-like 帚: picture arriving home and cleaning the dust away.",parts:[{glyph:"刂","label":"Doorway posts (left)","description":"The two upright strokes look like a narrow entrance. In this memory picture they become the doorway you walk through on the way home."},{glyph:"ヨ","label":"Broom / hand (right, top)","description":"The comb-like top shape can be pictured as a hand gripping a broom before sweeping the room."},{glyph:"冖","label":"House roof (right, middle)","description":"The short cover-shaped strokes look like the roof sheltering the home."},{glyph:"巾","label":"Hanging cloth (right, bottom)","description":"The lower hanging shape resembles a towel or apron waiting inside the doorway."}],story:"You walk through the doorway made by 刂 and step beneath the roof 冖. A towel 巾 is waiting inside to wipe the road dust from your hands, and you take the broom-shaped ヨ to sweep the floor because you have finally come home. The whole homecoming scene helps you remember 帰, return or go back.",words:[{word:"帰る",reading:"かえる",meaning:"to return; to go home"},{word:"帰国",reading:"きこく",meaning:"return to one’s home country"},{word:"帰り",reading:"かえり",meaning:"the way home; return trip"}]},
  "兄":{summary:"兄 puts a mouth 口 above two legs 儿: picture the older brother standing up to call everyone together.",parts:[{glyph:"口","label":"Mouth at the top","description":"The small box is 口, a mouth. Imagine the older sibling speaking first to get the family’s attention."},{glyph:"儿","label":"Two legs below","description":"The lower strokes look like a pair of legs. Picture the brother standing firmly in front."}],story:"A mouth 口 calls from above a pair of legs 儿. Imagine the older brother standing ahead and calling his younger siblings to follow. That leading voice and position help you remember 兄 as older brother.",words:[{word:"兄",reading:"あに",meaning:"older brother (one’s own)"},{word:"兄弟",reading:"きょうだい",meaning:"siblings; brothers"}]},
  "姉":{summary:"姉 places 女 beside a tall sign-like shape: picture an older sister standing by a height mark, taller than the younger children.",parts:[{glyph:"女","label":"Girl / woman","description":"The left side is 女, the familiar shape for a woman or girl."},{glyph:"市","label":"Tall sign shape","description":"The right side has a top canopy, a long upright stroke, and a crossbar. Picture it as a height mark reaching above the girl."}],story:"Picture a girl 女 standing beside a tall height mark. Her head reaches higher than the younger children beside her, so she is the older sister. The woman shape and tall marker make a simple memory for 姉.",words:[{word:"姉",reading:"あね",meaning:"older sister (one’s own)"},{word:"姉妹",reading:"しまい",meaning:"sisters"}]},
  "弟":{summary:"弟 opens with 八 like two arms reaching out; the bent lower strokes make a path for the younger brother to follow.",parts:[{glyph:"八","label":"Two open arms","description":"The two short strokes at the top spread apart like arms reaching to either side."},{glyph:"弓","label":"Bent bow shape","description":"The lower strokes bend like a bow. Picture the curve as the younger sibling following along behind the outstretched arms."}],story:"At the top, 八 opens like two arms. Imagine an older sibling holding both arms out for a younger brother to catch up. The long, bent strokes below make a path for the little brother to follow close behind. This scene helps you remember 弟 as younger brother.",words:[{word:"弟",reading:"おとうと",meaning:"younger brother (one’s own)"},{word:"兄弟",reading:"きょうだい",meaning:"siblings; brothers"}]},
  "妹":{summary:"妹 puts 女 beside 未, a tree-like shape whose top branch is still short: picture a young girl who has not grown as tall yet.",parts:[{glyph:"女","label":"Girl / woman","description":"The left side is 女, the familiar shape for a woman or girl."},{glyph:"未","label":"Not-yet tree shape","description":"The right side looks like a small tree with a shorter upper branch. 未 can mean ‘not yet’; use that idea for someone still growing."}],story:"Picture a young girl 女 beside a little tree 未 whose upper branch has not grown tall yet. The girl is still growing, so she is the younger sister. The girl and not-yet-grown tree help you remember 妹.",words:[{word:"妹",reading:"いもうと",meaning:"younger sister (one’s own)"},{word:"姉妹",reading:"しまい",meaning:"sisters"}]}
});
